<title>GERMANY: Leffers, Sinn set merger terms.</title>
<headline>Leffers, Sinn set merger terms.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>German textile groups Leffers AG and Sinn AG announced on Monday terms of their previously-announced merger.</p>
<p>The companies said three Leffers shares, which have a nominal value of 50 marks, will be exchanged for two Sinn shares, which also have a nominal value of 50 marks.</p>
<p>A payment of 1.16 marks will also be issued for each Leffers share.</p>
<p>Both Leffers and Sinn, which announced their intention for the merger in March, are part of the diversified trading group Schickedanz.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
